{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Hessian Matrix.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Hessian Matrix.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"hessian matrix hessian matrix","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Hessian Matrix.md","fileName":"Hessian Matrix.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Hessian Matrix","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 19:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Optimization and Differentiation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Optimization and Differentiation","Symmetric Matrix","Stationary Point","Local Minimum","Local Maximum","Saddle Point","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Hessian Matrix.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Hessian Matrix.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"hessian matrix hessian matrix","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Hessian Matrix.md","fileName":"Hessian Matrix.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Hessian Matrix","heading":"Hessian Matrix","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The Hessian matrix of a twice-differentiable function collects its second partial derivatives: $H_{ij}=\\partial^2f/(\\partial x_i\\partial x_j)$. When mixed partials agree, the Hessian is a [[Symmetric Matrix]].\n\nAt a [[Stationary Point]], a positive-definite Hessian indicates a strict [[Local Minimum]], and a negative-definite Hessian indicates a strict [[Local Maximum]]. An indefinite Hessian is associated with a [[Saddle Point]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Optimization and Differentiation","Symmetric Matrix","Stationary Point","Local Minimum","Local Maximum","Saddle Point","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Hessian Matrix.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Hessian Matrix.md","sourceType":"markd